<title>USA: Powell files suit against Erly executives.</title>
<headline>Powell files suit against Erly executives.</headline>
<dateline>BATON ROUGE, La. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Powell Group, which owns a stake in Erly Industries Inc, said on Thursday that it has filed a lawsuit against two officers of Erly, alleging a breach of fiduciary duty.</p>
<p>Powell and its president Naette Kelley own a 3.8 percent interest in Erly and filed the suit in the U.S. District Court for the Central District of California against Erly chairman and chief executive Gerald Murphy and chief operating officer Douglas Murphy, Powell said.</p>
<p>Erly was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
